/*
 * WHAT MAY BE READ FROM FLASH - the read-only twin of
 * default_text_excludes.incl, and the easier of the two.
 *
 * Named here means flash; left out means RAM.  Empty for stage 1, so
 * nothing has moved yet.
 *
 * Constant tables are the cheapest win available: they are read, never
 * written, and most are touched at human speed.  font1 alone is 2,680
 * bytes and the keyboard maps are more.  The ones to leave in RAM are
 * those read per pixel or per scanline - gfx_lut is built at run time
 * so it is .data and never a candidate, but anything the expanders
 * touch on the scanout path belongs in RAM whatever it is.
 *
 * Note that with -fdata-sections each object gets .rodata.<name>, so
 * this is per table, by name.
 */
